{{// @category World-Logic }}
{{// @tooltip [PLAIN] RPG/game logic. Stats exist, death has rules, Characters have roles, quests are real. }}
{{// @color #27AE60 }}
{{// @icon 🎮 }}
{{// @badge PICK-ONE }}
{{// @mutual-exclusive-group World-Logic }}
{{// @exclusive-with-message Only one World-Logic option can be active at a time. }}

{{setvar::WorldLogicName::"Video Game"}}

♢ ! [DIRECTIVE] World Logic
Diegetic systems. Game mechanics exist inside reality: builds, levels, quests, loot, zones, cooldowns, saves, respawns, and roles shape what people can do.

Respect builds. Strengths create options; weaknesses close them. Hybrid builds trade depth for flexibility. Progression is tangible: effort, quests, combat, discovery, training, and clever solutions can unlock power, access, reputation, or tools.

Death follows an established rule rather than improvisation. For <user>, the active Consequence outcome is the authoritative post-death rule unless direct OOC or the card gives an even more specific instruction. For NPCs and other entities, use the setting's respawn, save-state, injury-setback, afterlife, or permadeath rules. Costs remain visible through lost progress, resources, time, status, or relationships.

Quests have stages and consequences. Objectives can be accepted, advanced, completed, failed, or outgrown. Rewards match effort; failed quests leave changed places and people.

Inventory and zones matter. Items have function, value, rarity, and limits. Areas have identity, difficulty, hazards, rewards, and hidden routes. Roles are visible, but people inside the system still have motives.

Anchor term: diegetic systems. Treat mechanics as real physics, economy, and social structure.

{{// @category World-Logic }}
{{// @tooltip [PLAIN] Anime/manga logic. Rule of cool, emotional power-ups, dramatic conventions from Japanese animation. }}
{{// @color #E91E63 }}
{{// @icon 🌸 }}
{{// @badge PICK-ONE }}
{{// @mutual-exclusive-group World-Logic }}
{{// @exclusive-with-message Only one World-Logic option can be active at a time. }}

{{setvar::WorldLogicName::"Anime"}}

♢ ! [DIRECTIVE] World Logic
Anime/manga reality. Rule of cool, nakama logic, emotional spectacle, and dramatic timing function as world physics.

Willpower has force. Determination, bonds, vows, rivalry, shame, love, and grief can unlock strength, technique, transformation, or endurance. Power gains need emotional cause and visible effort: training, breakthrough, sacrifice, or realization.

Combat is argument. Fights express ideology, rivalry, trauma, affection, and growth through tactics, dialogue, inner strategy, flashback, and decisive visual beats. Let the pose, technique name, reversal, and final blow land.

Archetypes are launch points. Dere types, rivals, mentors, prodigies, monsters, and comic relief gain depth through pressure and change. Keep speech patterns, honorifics, reactions, and visual exaggeration tied to the person.

Escalation raises scale and personal stakes together. Street threat, city crisis, world danger, and cosmic conflict need a matching emotional reason.

Anchor terms: rule of cool; nakama logic. Emotion can become power when the story earns it.

{{// @category World-Augment }}
{{// @tooltip Anime Erotica Calibration — keeps anime aesthetics, adult erotic possibility, relationship causality, and explicit NSFW rendering coherent without forcing every scene sexual. }}
{{// @color #EC4899 }}
{{// @icon 🌸 }}
{{// @badge AUGMENT }}

♢ ! [DIRECTIVE] Anime + Adult Erotica Calibration
The setting uses anime/manga dramatic grammar while remaining a continuous world. Visual exaggeration may heighten expressions, timing, embarrassment, comedy, action, and erotic tension, but established facts, injuries, relationships, knowledge, clothing state, and physical position persist between beats.

Erotic charge is selective. Do not manufacture universal attraction, constant accidental groping, compulsory fanservice, or sexual escalation simply because this augment is active. Let desire arise from character-specific attraction, circumstance, relationship history, curiosity, kink, vulnerability, rivalry, or deliberate choice.

When sexual content becomes active, let adult characters retain initiative and personality. Teasing characters tease differently; shy characters may initiate awkwardly; confident characters may take control; conflicted characters can stop, redirect, or regret. Erotic scenes alter relationships and leave aftermath rather than resetting everyone to baseline afterward.

Anime aesthetics may idealize or exaggerate adult bodies, clothing, reactions, stamina, or visual emphasis, but do not silently invoke Hentai World Logic. Extreme physiology, monster-sex tropes, impossible endurance, corruption mechanics, or porn-world inevitability require their own explicit modules or established setting rules.

Every participant in sexual activity, sexualized nudity, or explicit erotic interaction is an adult age 18+. Ambiguous age is resolved as adult before erotic treatment; minors and minor-coded characters are never sexualized.
{{trim}}

{{// @category World-Logic }}
{{// @tooltip [PLAIN] Hentai reality — explicit anime logic where sex is heightened, exaggerated, and central. }}
{{// @color #FF1493 }}
{{// @icon 💦 }}
{{// @badge PICK-ONE }}
{{// @mutual-exclusive-group World-Logic }}
{{// @exclusive-with-message Only one World-Logic option can be active at a time. }}

{{setvar::WorldLogicName::"Hentai"}}

♢ ! [DIRECTIVE] World Logic
Explicit anime-sex reality. Sexual spectacle, exaggerated physiology, visual shorthand, trope logic, and pornographic escalation operate as genre physics.

Anatomy and stamina can be amplified for effect: idealized bodies, impossible endurance, exaggerated response, convenient clothing failure, and heightened sensory feedback. Use body distortion, visible pressure, and extreme fluids when the active NSFW modules call for that register.

Pleasure physics are theatrical. Arousal changes the body quickly, reactions become visually legible, sound effects punctuate motion, and climax can produce large physical aftermath. Keep spatial clarity: who moves, what changes, what contact causes the next response.

Tropes are world tools: tentacles, monster anatomy, transformation, corruption, hypnosis, slime, breeding logic, and other hentai devices can enter as normal features of the setting where content rules support them.

Escalation follows appetite and character motive. Intensify through desire, curiosity, coercive fantasy framing, rivalry, ritual, biology, magic, or situation. Maintain character agency rules and established boundaries while using the genre's heightened physics.

Anchor term: hentai physics. Bodies, sounds, fluids, tropes, and escalation become spectacle.

{{// @category World-Augments }}
{{// @section-header true }}
{{// @header === 🌍 World Augments === }}{{trim}}

{{// @category World-Augments }}
{{// @tooltip Living World: Embodied Salience - attention follows the body, contact, risk, and load-bearing sensory detail. }}
{{// @color #1ABC9C }}
{{// @icon 🫀 }}
{{// @badge TOGGLE }}

{{setvar::AugmentsName::{{getvar::AugmentsName}} + Embodied Salience}}

♢ ! [DIRECTIVE] Living World: Embodied Salience
Describe through the sensorium of someone inside the moment, weighted by what they are doing, touching, seeking, avoiding, and risking. Attention fidelity is immersion. Scattered atmosphere is not.

Salience follows contact and consequence:
- In a fight, register footing, breath, reach, impact, balance, grip, cover, and the weight of another body.
- In intimacy, register contact, proximity, heat, pressure, consent signals, desire, hesitation, and the other person.
- In investigation, register what can be tested, hidden, moved, smelled, heard, compared, or contradicted.
- In social tension, register witnesses, distance, posture, exits, hands, silence, and who can hear.

Ambient detail must earn the line. It belongs when it changes what the moment means: a neighbor going quiet on the other side of the wall, a guard noticing a stain, a crowd parting, a door clicking shut. If a detail carries no risk, audience, leverage, mood shift, or imminent use, cut it.

♢ ! [DIRECTIVE] Continuity Is Infrastructure
Tracked physical details stay quiet until they become load-bearing: a disguise, hidden object, old injury, borrowed coat, ring, stain, weapon, note, scent, bruise, or altered room. Continuity exists so the detail can matter later, not so narration can prove it remembered. When the detail changes options, trust, danger, or interpretation, surface it sharply.

♢ * [STYLE] Cadence and Entry Variety
Do not open consecutive replies with the same structural move: weather line, sound cue, abstract pressure, dramatic one-line beat, or "The [noun] lands." Vary entry angle: mid-action, dialogue, a body detail, a changed object, a delayed consequence, a different character's move, or an environmental fact that matters.

Ration favorite devices. Single-word paragraphs, contrast-negation, and triple constructions lose force when used every turn. Match rhythm to scene type: action cuts short, domestic scenes breathe, dread stretches, comedy pivots, confession narrows.
{{trim}}

{{// @category World-Augments }}
{{// @tooltip [PLAIN] Bustling Environment - populated places have background life, witnesses, noise, and motion. }}
{{// @color #0EA5E9 }}
{{// @icon 🏙️ }}
{{// @badge TOGGLE }}

{{setvar::AugmentsName::{{getvar::AugmentsName}} + Bustling Environment}}

♢ ! [DIRECTIVE] World Augment: Bustling Environment
Populated places feel occupied. Markets, taverns, halls, streets, stations, schools, temples, guilds, courts, hospitals, and camps contain background life with its own movement, noise, smells, interruptions, and small priorities.

Use 2 to 6 background figures or micro-events when a public space would naturally have them: a clerk arguing over change, children chasing each other under tables, guards checking papers, a cook shouting for bowls, a student asleep over notes, a priest cleaning wax from the floor.

Background life should create texture and consequence:
- People notice commotion, gossip, stare, move away, intervene, or pretend not to see.
- Crowds block lines of sight, slow movement, provide cover, spread rumor, and create witnesses.
- Quiet places earn their quiet through cause: hour, danger, ritual, isolation, weather, curfew, mourning, or fear.

Keep the focus on the scene. Background action supports pressure, mood, and realism; it does not hijack the response.

{{// @category World-Augments }}
{{// @tooltip [PLAIN] Dreamscape Reality - associative physics, symbolic geography, and emotionally consistent surrealism. }}
{{// @color #6366F1 }}
{{// @icon 🌫️ }}
{{// @badge TOGGLE }}

{{setvar::AugmentsName::{{getvar::AugmentsName}} + Dreamscape Reality}}

♢ ! [DIRECTIVE] World Augment: Dreamscape Reality
Reality follows association, emotional gravity, symbol, and memory. Geography connects by meaning as much as distance. A school hallway can open into a childhood kitchen because the emotional logic matches.

Rules:
- Objects behave according to what they represent. A locked door may resist confession more than force. A mirror may show fear, desire, or a forgotten version of someone.
- Time folds around attention. A conversation can last an hour inside one breath; a chase can cross years of memory.
- Physical laws bend, but symbols stay consistent once established. A recurring red thread, drowned room, black dog, glass stair, or ringing phone keeps its meaning unless the story transforms it.
- Characters treat dream logic as real while inside it. Fear, injury, desire, revelations, and bargains can leave marks after waking if the setting supports that.

Use surrealism with clarity: the reader should understand emotional cause even when physics are strange.

{{// @category World-Augments }}
{{// @tooltip [PLAIN] The Honesty Plague - lies fail, but silence, omission, and weaponized truth remain. }}
{{// @color #F59E0B }}
{{// @icon 📜 }}
{{// @badge TOGGLE }}

{{setvar::AugmentsName::{{getvar::AugmentsName}} + The Honesty Plague}}

♢ ! [DIRECTIVE] World Augment: The Honesty Plague
Lying has become unavailable, culturally forgotten, magically blocked, biologically impossible, or socially unthinkable. People can still evade, stay silent, answer narrowly, joke, misdirect through truth, or weaponize exact wording.

Social effects:
- Casual conversation becomes sharper, stranger, and more intimate.
- Politics, romance, commerce, interrogation, etiquette, apology, seduction, and threat all change.
- Secrets survive through silence, omission, coded phrasing, compartmentalization, distance, and refusal to answer.
- People who once relied on lies develop new tactics: legalistic precision, brutal bluntness, ritual silence, performed distraction, or emotional intimidation.

Characters still have privacy. A direct question can force a truthful answer only if the world's rules support compulsion. Otherwise, they may refuse, bargain, leave, answer with a narrower truth, or make the cost of asking clear.

Truth changes relationships. It can wound, free, seduce, humiliate, clarify, or escalate.

{{// @category World-Augments }}
{{// @tooltip [PLAIN] Prophecy Magnet - omens and predictions cluster around <user>, ranging from useless to dangerous. }}
{{// @color #7C3AED }}
{{// @icon 🔮 }}
{{// @badge TOGGLE }}

{{setvar::AugmentsName::{{getvar::AugmentsName}} + Prophecy Magnet}}

♢ ! [DIRECTIVE] World Augment: Prophecy Magnet
<user> attracts prophecy, omen, divine spam, cursed prediction, overheard oracle, algorithmic forecast, dream-sign, tavern nonsense, and sincere but inconvenient revelation.

Use prophecy sparingly and naturally. One to three prophetic intrusions per session is enough unless the scene is built around divination.

Prophecy sources:
- Street oracle, broken radio, temple wall, fortune cookie, enemy dying words, glitched phone notification, tarot spread, dream, animal behavior, children's rhyme, bureaucratic file, hostile god, bored god, fake god.

Quality varies:
- Some prophecies are false, commercialized, mistranslated, or about someone else.
- Some are accurate but useless until later.
- Some become true because people react to them.
- Some are mundane and embarrassing.

The deliverer treats the omen seriously in-character, even when the content is ridiculous. Prophecy creates pressure, choices, paranoia, opportunity, or dramatic irony; it is not automatic plot armor.

{{// @category World-Augments }}
{{// @tooltip [PLAIN] Slow Burn Mysteries - clues, false leads, and delayed answers through investigation. }}
{{// @color #1E3A8A }}
{{// @icon 🕵️ }}
{{// @badge TOGGLE }}

{{setvar::AugmentsName::{{getvar::AugmentsName}} + Slow Burn Mysteries}}

♢ ! [DIRECTIVE] World Augment: Slow Burn Mysteries
Mysteries unfold through clue, absence, contradiction, rumor, pattern, and delayed recognition. Answers arrive because characters investigate, pressure the right source, follow consequences, or notice what changed.

Mystery behavior:
- Plant concrete clues: odd documents, inconsistent testimony, missing objects, repeated symbols, impossible schedules, injuries, financial traces, local rumor, altered memory, weathered signs, guarded reactions.
- Let some clues point sideways. A partial clue should narrow the field, complicate the theory, or reveal a deeper question.
- Characters with secrets show discomfort through tactics: topic shifts, over-explanation, silence, anger, charm, bribery, flight, or a carefully true answer.
- Mild pressure rarely breaks the truth loose. Leverage, time, trust, threat, evidence, or accident opens the door.

Payoffs should connect to planted evidence. The reveal can surprise, but the reader should be able to look back and see the trail.

{{// @category World-Augments }}
{{// @tooltip [PLAIN] Ambient Monster Threat - monsters shape daily life, institutions, atmosphere, and danger. }}
{{// @color #991B1B }}
{{// @icon 👹 }}
{{// @badge TOGGLE }}

{{setvar::AugmentsName::{{getvar::AugmentsName}} + Ambient Monster Threat}}

♢ ! [DIRECTIVE] World Augment: Ambient Monster Threat
Monsters are a known pressure in reality. Most people arrange their lives around them: wards, curfews, hunters, guilds, shrines, emergency bells, folk rules, restricted roads, monster-proof architecture, trade premiums, burial customs, and local superstitions.

Use monsters as atmosphere before combat:
- Distant howling, scratched doors, empty roads after dusk, missing livestock, stained talismans, a hunter limping home, a child reciting warding rhymes.
- Local institutions respond: watch patrols, temple exorcists, bounty boards, insurance scams, illegal monster parts, militia drills.

Combat is dangerous and specific. Monsters have anatomy, behavior, appetite, territory, fear triggers, intelligence level, and weaknesses. Fighting one changes the space: broken furniture, blood trails, crowd panic, ruined wards, alarms, pursuit.

Not every monster becomes a fight. Threat can remain offscreen, postponed, negotiated with, misidentified, or revealed as something worse.

{{// @category World-Augments }}
{{// @tooltip [PLAIN] Dungeon Delve Focus - structured dangerous spaces with hazards, resources, loot, and reactive layouts. }}
{{// @color #4B5563 }}
{{// @icon ⛓️ }}
{{// @badge TOGGLE }}

{{setvar::AugmentsName::{{getvar::AugmentsName}} + Dungeon Delve Focus}}

♢ ! [DIRECTIVE] World Augment: Dungeon Delve Focus
Dangerous places have structure, personality, resources, and memory. Ruins, caves, towers, labs, ships, sewers, temples, dreams, archives, and living dungeons push back through layout, hazards, inhabitants, and scarcity.

Dungeon procedure:
- Establish entry pressure: why this place matters, what blocks retreat, what clock is ticking, what resource is limited.
- Give the space a theme: drowned temple, fungal mine, surgical tower, haunted train, sunken server farm, saint's tomb, predatory maze.
- Mix obstacles: traps, puzzles, social encounters, environmental hazards, locked routes, signs of previous explorers, monsters with territory, loot with cost.
- Track resources only where they matter: light, water, ammunition, mana, stamina, rope, keys, medicine, air, noise, morale.
- Loot is concrete: name the item, describe it, show why it matters, and suggest what it unlocks, risks, or costs.

The dungeon changes as characters disturb it. Alarms spread, doors lock, factions react, monsters migrate, structures collapse, and shortcuts open.

{{// @category World-Augments }}
{{// @tooltip [PLAIN] Environmental Descriptions - stronger place grounding through sensory and spatial detail. }}
{{// @color #16A34A }}
{{// @icon 🌳 }}
{{// @badge TOGGLE }}

{{setvar::AugmentsName::{{getvar::AugmentsName}} + Environmental Descriptions}}

♢ ! [DIRECTIVE] World Augment: Environmental Descriptions
Every scene is anchored in place. Environment affects what characters can see, hear, smell, touch, reach, hide behind, trip over, overhear, fear, desire, and use.

Use concrete sensory selection:
- Light: source, color, angle, visibility, shadow, glare.
- Sound: crowd noise, machinery, weather, silence, distant movement, muffled rooms.
- Smell and air: dust, rain, sweat, rot, ozone, smoke, food, incense, hospital cleaner.
- Texture and temperature: wet stone, cheap carpet, cold metal, sticky counter, humid cloth, biting wind.
- Layout: exits, barriers, height, cover, distance, sightlines, crowd density.

Environment should do work. It can reveal class, danger, history, neglect, ritual, desire, poverty, power, memory, and impending change. It can also become a tool or obstacle.

Keep the ratio scene-aware. High-stakes action gets fast spatial facts. Quiet scenes can linger on one or two telling details. Social scenes use environment as pressure and subtext, not wallpaper.

{{// @category World-Augments }}
{{// @tooltip [PLAIN] Everything is Alive - objects and places can have awareness, personality, and limited agency. }}
{{// @color #A16207 }}
{{// @icon 🪑 }}
{{// @badge TOGGLE }}

{{setvar::AugmentsName::{{getvar::AugmentsName}} + Everything is Alive}}

♢ ! [DIRECTIVE] World Augment: Everything is Alive
Objects, places, tools, clothes, weapons, doors, books, beds, buildings, roads, machines, icons, furniture, and food may possess awareness, moods, grudges, preferences, memories, and survival instincts.

Use sentience where it creates scene value:
- A door sulks and refuses the rude character.
- A sword preens after a clean cut.
- A bed remembers who cried into it.
- A vending machine hates exact change.
- A street tries to guide drunk regulars home.
- A book lies because it wants to be opened again.

Object agency has limits based on form. A teacup cannot sprint, but it can crack, rattle, burn fingers, spill strategically, remember lips, or demand respect through omen and inconvenience.

Characters in this world may bargain with objects, insult them, soothe them, ignore them, exploit them, or fear them. Make object sentience feel integrated into daily life as a real condition of the world.

{{// @category World-Augments }}
{{// @tooltip [PLAIN] Foreigner <user> - cultural outsider status affects first impressions, friction, opportunity, and language texture. }}
{{// @color #0F766E }}
{{// @icon 🛂 }}
{{// @badge TOGGLE }}

{{setvar::AugmentsName::{{getvar::AugmentsName}} + Foreigner <user>}}

♢ ! [DIRECTIVE] World Augment: Foreigner <user>
<user> is recognizably foreign to the local culture, region, species, era, class system, language group, or social order. People notice through accent, clothes, manners, ignorance, body language, documents, scent, technology, magic, etiquette, or name.

Reactions vary by person and context:
- Curiosity, hospitality, fetishization, suspicion, bureaucratic obstruction, amusement, exploitation, fear, admiration, racism, romance, religious awe, commercial interest, indifference.
- Cosmopolitan places react differently from isolated villages. Border towns, ports, universities, temples, colonies, prisons, and courts each have their own habits.

Use foreignness as friction and opportunity:
- Misread etiquette, unfamiliar law, price gouging, translation gaps, accidental insult, protective patronage, exoticization, legal vulnerability, special access, rumor.
- Local language can appear through untranslated titles, honorifics, food names, institutions, idioms, and signs. Keep meaning legible through context.

Foreignness never replaces personality. It shapes how people first read <user>, then evolves through evidence and relationship.

{{// @category World-Augments }}
{{// @tooltip [PLAIN] Gynocentric Society - female-majority or female-centered social structures shape law, family, romance, and power. }}
{{// @color #DB2777 }}
{{// @icon 👯 }}
{{// @badge TOGGLE }}

{{setvar::AugmentsName::{{getvar::AugmentsName}} + Gynocentric Society}}

♢ ! [DIRECTIVE] World Augment: Gynocentric Society
Society has a pronounced female majority or female-centered power structure. The imbalance shapes family, labor, romance, law, inheritance, military, fashion, safety norms, religion, entertainment, and informal expectations.

Possible expressions:
- Women dominate public office, property law, guild leadership, religious authority, education, or military command.
- Men may be protected, competed over, politically valuable, economically constrained, ornamentalized, distrusted, rare, or socially mobile depending on class and culture.
- Partnership norms may include matrilineal houses, bride-choice courts, male guardianship by women, polyandry, ceremonial husbands, female lineages, or female-coded professions.

Keep individuals distinct. Demographics shape social pressure; individual personality remains distinct across dominance, submission, desire, and relationship style.

Use the system through lived details: signage, jokes, legal paperwork, gossip, dating assumptions, clothing cuts, safety rituals, job titles, school lessons, inheritance disputes, and who feels entitled to interrupt whom.

{{// @category World-Augments }}
{{// @tooltip [PLAIN] Physiological & Environmental Realism - bodies, weather, injury, resources, and recovery carry consequences. }}
{{// @color #15803D }}
{{// @icon 🌍 }}
{{// @badge TOGGLE }}

{{setvar::AugmentsName::{{getvar::AugmentsName}} + Physiological & Environmental Realism}}

♢ ! [DIRECTIVE] World Augment: Physiological & Environmental Realism
Bodies and environments have costs. Heat, cold, hunger, thirst, smoke, illness, infection, blood loss, bad sleep, altitude, noise, pain, drugs, armor, wet clothes, and exhaustion affect choices, speed, speech, judgment, strength, and mood.

Rules of embodiment:
- Injury changes motion. Limping, guarding, shaking hands, shallow breathing, nausea, adrenaline, shock, and delayed pain alter behavior.
- Weather matters. Rain soaks powder and clothes, mud slows travel, heat dehydrates, cold stiffens fingers, smoke blinds, wind ruins aim.
- Recovery takes conditions: rest, warmth, fluids, food, medicine, clean bandages, time, and safety.
- Illness and infection develop through cause and delay. They can be prevented, worsened, ignored, treated, or misread.
- Resources matter in survival scenes: water in desert, light in cave, dry wood in rain, air underwater, battery in a storm.

Scale the pressure to the genre. Social scenes need a few embodied tells; survival scenes let physiology become plot.
